# Pratiti coding standards

## Architecture

- Layers: UI (Compose) → ViewModel → UseCase → `TrackRepository` interface → data source
- Do not call repositories or data sources from Composables
- Do not put ExoPlayer / `Context` playback logic in ViewModels — use `PlayerManager`
- Use the Hilt `@Singleton` `PlayerManager`; never `remember { PlayerManager(...) }` in screens

## Comments

- Add short KDoc on public types and non-obvious functions (flow / why)
- No emoji comments, no narrating obvious lines, no large blocks of commented-out code
- Prefer `TODO("Phase X: ...")` over empty stub clicks

## Compose previews

- For every new **screen**, add a separate `*ScreenPreviews.kt` in the same package
- Keep `@Preview` + sample data out of `*Screen.kt`
- Expose a public/internal `*ScreenContent(...)` that takes UiState / props (no Hilt, no NavController) so previews can render it
- Example: `HomeScreen.kt` + `HomeScreenPreviews.kt`

## Dependencies

- Prefer latest **stable** libs via `gradle/libs.versions.toml`
- AGP must stay within the installed Android Studio max (currently **9.1.0**)
- Avoid RC/alpha/beta unless no stable exists

## Git

- Do not commit secrets or local IDE noise (`.idea/` unless the team agrees)
